task.claim:
For each of the 3 curves of
research/endosweep_dk_exact_batch3_20261017/dk_exact.json (other/E-382,
nums/numsp384t1, arkworks/bw6_761), with p, t, h, n, D_K, f, s and the factorisation as
recorded there:
  p + 1 - t = h*n;
  t^2 - 4p = D_K * f^2;
  4p - t^2 = prod p_i^e_i (the factorisation certificate);
  the odd-exponent p_i multiply to s, and D_K = -s or -4*s as
    nist.exact_discriminant computes it; D_K is a discriminant;
  min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) is the recorded value, 2^L <= |D_K| < 2^(L+1)
    and min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) >= 2^(L-2);
  and, if the listed factors above 10^8 are prime, D_K is a fundamental
    discriminant.
Moreover D_K = -3 on arkworks/bw6_761, and on the other 2 curves
|D_K| >= 2^381 and min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) >= 2^379.
